1
00:00:01,010 --> 00:04:27,050
Part 7 stopped on the company of Kamsa. Then the Lord saw, and all the boys saw. The boys saw a great creature standing there. Sattva means a living being, an animal. An astonishing animal, vast, and still. Still means it was not moving. They understood it was a living being, and it was motionless. The moment they saw it, the children were distressed. A great bright bird, like the peak of a mountain. They will be afraid on seeing it. They could not run, and they could not keep standing either. They became frightened. What now. They were only thinking, and by then it had come and swallowed Krishna in a snatch. It was like a mountain peak broken by a thunderbolt. Indra had struck with the thunderbolt, and the peaks of mountains had fallen here and there. It seemed a mountain peak had fallen from the sky. Maharaj Parikshit asked in his mind, who was that, please tell. The children did not know, but you know. Shukadeva says, that great demon was named Baka, and he had taken the form of a crane. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.11.48] His name was Baka from before. And Putana herself is called Baki. Ah, that Baki. Putana's name was Baki, and his name also was Baka. To settle this score, Aghasura came as a python. That katha is after this chapter. Just now this one had swallowed the Lord. A great demon means very strong. He had taken the form of a crane. The children were afraid. They were not running, and they were not staying. They were trembling.

2
00:04:29,270 --> 00:09:15,840
Suddenly. If Krishna, or the boys of Braj, had known that this one would run to eat them, they would have fled. They could not guess it, so the word sahasa, suddenly, is used. It was sitting quietly, and then all at once it moved with speed and swallowed Krishna. A true rush, one morsel, and Krishna was eaten. It was strong. At that same moment they fell, fainted, as the senses become when the life is gone. Seeing Krishna eaten, all began to cry out. They could not cry out for long either. Now the belief was fixed: Krishna has gone into the belly. Krishna is so dear that how shall we live without him. The moment they thought this, they became like lifeless. They were not speaking. They fell. Seeing this misery of his friends, the Lord at once came out of its mouth. When it had taken the Lord into its mouth, it had taken him in with the beak, not into the belly. Krishna was already in front of the beak. It thought, he will be swallowed straight. When he reached the root of the palate, he began to taste bitter. Prabhupada says the Lord is sweeter than sugar. Here he began to feel as if red-hot iron had been swallowed. The root of the palate burned intensely. It had swallowed him with the mouth wide open, and it also vomited. Still the anger did not stop. There was no hole in the body, no wound. So soft a body, and nowhere a hole. It came into its mind, this is a very dangerous thing. Now I will strike with the beak. Inside, there was no question of deciding anymore. It seemed he was a ball of fire. Like iron heated by fire.

3
00:09:15,840 --> 00:13:59,920
One acharya says, fire is called Krishna-vartma. Krishna-vartma is a name of fire. Fire, from the name of the Lord. I am the shelter of fire. Fire rests on Me. Manifest a little of your own fire and burn its throat. Krishna naturally became hot. In a moment the Lord can be cooler than the moon, and more burning than the sun. There was still fear: after all it has a body, and he is so fiercely hot, how shall I strike. Still it thought of striking with the beak. It was opening the beak again and again, from a little way off. Now fear was coming. At that same moment Sri Krishna ran, caught both beaks with both hands, and before the eyes of the children tore them into two pieces. The upper beak and the lower. Having torn them, he threw the two pieces this way and that. The whole body split, not the beak alone. He began from the beak, and threw the two pieces apart like a vegetable. The children became very happy. One acharya writes, why did the Lord go into its mouth, why did he come out, and why tear the beak, why not kill it another way. The Lord thought, the one whose breast I drank, she is my mother. She had become that much a mother. And this is a brother of my mother's brother. The moment the word mama, uncle, came, the memory of Kamsa came, and in that anger he tore him. In the next verse it is said that Krishna is the husband of the devotees, their protector, and this Bakasura is Kamsa's friend. One meaning they give: he tore him like a reed, like a soft straw. Like bamboo. The meaning is, a relative of Kamsa is my enemy, so tearing him like bamboo the Lord is saying, I am the one who will finish the whole family. Not Bakasura alone. I will end the whole line. No name and no trace left. He is giving notice that the line will be finished completely. Before the eyes of the children, in play, as a lila. He made no effort. The gods were watching. Increasing the joy of the gods, he tore him like soft grass.

4
00:14:01,160 --> 00:17:28,160
The joy of the gods grew great. The gods were very pleased by the killing of Bakasura, and he is describing their pleasure. The residents of the world of the gods began to rain the malati and other flowers of the Nandana forest. The flower malati is very dear to Lord Krishna and Balarama. They knew this is dear to the Lord. They were ready with the flowers of the malati creepers in the Nandana forest, or they brought them at once and rained them. The flowers of heaven are much larger than those of this earth, and completely light in weight. They began to rain flowers, and not the rain alone. They began to praise, to offer prayers. They began to sound the drums, to sound the conches, and to offer beautiful praise. Here, its dying, Krishna coming out of the belly, the tearing of it, and from above the flowers and the sound. The children of the cowherds fell into great wonder. What is happening. He is something of the Lord, that is what is wanted, so they fell into wonder. This wonder was born of joy. A rain of flowers is falling on our friend. It succeeded. He won. We had understood that he died, that he went into its belly, and he came back. He came out of its throat. In a moment the gods can sing any thing in a poem, in a song. They began to sing the song of Bakasura. What lila had just happened, that they began to sing. The children became very pleased. There is a wonder of joy, and a wonder of sorrow. This was the wonder of joy. Having found him freed from the mouth of the crane, life came into them again.

5
00:17:29,600 --> 00:21:46,820
They stood up so quickly, on seeing Krishna, that it seemed life had suddenly come into the body. Where they had fallen unconscious, they came out and took Krishna into their arms. They became very happy. The children began to embrace him, began to look at him, is there any scratch on the body. The beak had struck him, it had taken him inside, there was the fear of a cut, and nowhere was blood coming. Nowhere a swelling. He was completely well. Balarama took him in his arms. All the children took him in their arms. Now drive the calves, and they set off running for Vraja, for home. Coming into Vraja, they began to sing it. Singing means, with great wonder, and they began to tell it many times. There was a creature like a crane. It came. It had swallowed Krishna. How the Lord made him come out. He came out of the mouth. The children are telling the event for the first time. Jagu means to sing. Many times. In every house they began to tell it, to sing it. Hearing this, the cowherd men and the gopis gathered in groups wherever they were. They were hearing, what happened. Everyone had great honor toward Krishna, affection. They all began to accept that Krishna had died and come back, had gone to another world and returned. Come back from death. All their eyes were thirsty. They were looking at their dear Krishna with thirsty eyes. First all took him in their arms, and after that they began to look with love. In looking at Krishna the eyes are not satisfied. A person to whom you give water, and even after the giving the thirst does not go, and he keeps drinking. In this way they began to look at Krishna. With great attention, has any cut gone into the body. And they were accepting that Krishna had received life again. When the children said, it took him fully into the belly, it ate him, and how he came out, the Lord's mercy is astonishing, all became greatly amazed. Here and there they began to talk. What troubles are coming upon this child. And Lord Narayana is saving him.

6
00:21:48,100 --> 00:28:47,420
So what do the cowherds say among themselves. In three verses Shukadeva Goswami says, ah, this child has had many deaths. Death means, the causes of death came. Causes came that were able to kill. Many times the causes of this child's death came, and the same one died. It did not happen that anyone fled from here. Whoever came to kill, that one died. This Bakasura also has just died. Not that he flies away from the danger of Krishna. He came to kill, and he died. In past births they will have given fear to others, will have tormented them. Otherwise how do they die by colliding with a child. They died by their own karma. Their feeling could not be that Krishna killed them. They will have given pain, will have tormented living beings, so Brahma will have written, on this day, in this place, let the life go. Let them die by their bad karma. Someone came to Braj on a journey, a young body, and suddenly death happens. A man thinks, what is the cause, was there a disease. In Braj no one killed them. The children were grazing calves, were drinking water. There was no means. And coming, they themselves are dying. They have given pain to others, they have done sin, and by that sin they are dying. And if some child comes and says, Krishna tore its beak, they say, no, no. All died by their own sin. Where is such power in a child. They never accepted that Krishna has done something. All the acts were happening in so natural a way. How to accept it. The child whom Bakasura ate, can anyone accept that the child will tear its beak. How he came out, the people did not know. They will have asked, how did you come out, how did it vomit you. The Lord will have told them, I do not know what the matter was, it seemed its mouth burned. When Krishna came, then they saw this. They did not see him coming out of the mouth. This is a thing of great wonder. But the cowherds were speaking their own thoughts on this event. Demons of dreadful sight came, at the seeing of whom the heart can be struck. The form was that terrible. They tried to kill the child, and still the child did not die. They come here to kill him, and they are destroyed like a moth in the fire. What mercy of Lord Narayana. Let everyone worship the Lord. In one place there is fire, and thousands of moths keep coming and being burned. To come near him is to die. Putana came, and she died. Trinavarta, the cart, the falling of the trees. They keep repeating all of this thousands of times. Night and day this is what they do. Only the talk of Krishna. And it is fresh news. The children have just come and said, he has come just now from killing. Several cowherds will have gone with courage to see. Come, let us see. Are they lying, are they telling the truth.

7
00:28:47,580 --> 00:33:23,740
Then they say, ah, the words of those who know Brahman are never untrue. What the worshipper Garga said of the Lord, that is exactly so. What the worshippers of the Lord say, what those who know the Veda say, and what the learned devotees of the Lord say, their words can never be untrue. Look, what Gargacharya had said, as he said it, is completely right. He had said, equal to Narayana in qualities. This child is full of qualities like Narayana. Equal to Narayana in qualities. It has become completely clear. A question comes, had Nanda Baba told the words of Gargacharya. Nanda Baba is so simple, of so straight a heart, that he does not hide them from his own people. He told them. Everyone kept asking about the child, so what should he say. He quoted it straight, Sripad Gargacharya said this. Now everyone says, look, what Gargacharya says cannot be untrue. One who knows Brahman, who knows Vishnu. The word of a Vaishnava, of those who know the Veda, can never be untrue. And a blessing given by brahmanas can never fail. Whatever brahmanas were in Braj, they would say to Krishna, live long, be without disease, be healthy, be happy. All these cowherd men and gopis accept that this is the blessing given by the brahmanas, so the child is healthy, nothing of his is going wrong. They did not know that a brahmana gives this same blessing, whether to Brahma or to everyone. By his mercy, Brahma, the husband of the brahmanas, creates. One who will be equal to Narayana in quality, one who will love him, enemies will not be able to defeat. But when the last verse was remembered, they would say, Nanda Maharaj, keep the child very protected. The cowherds are the same. All say, he is equal to Narayana in qualities. Its real meaning was that Narayana alone can be equal to him in qualities, and no one else. And they are taking this very much, equal to Narayana in qualities. Still they say, he must be kept very protected. Do not send the children alone to graze the calves. Let some mature cowherd go, with bow and arrow, and protect. Sending them alone like this is not right. And the other thing, they were following Krishna's pleasure. This is what all began to say.

8
00:33:23,740 --> 00:39:09,670
In this way Nanda and the other cowherds, joyfully telling and enjoying the katha of Krishna and Rama, did not find the pain of worldly life. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.11] In this way Nanda and the cowherds, night and day, kept speaking only the katha of Krishna and Rama. The meaning of katha is not that people do it by arranging a program. Ordinary talk is also called katha. It is not only in a gathering that this is called katha. Someone is talking, and they say, what katha are you doing. They do say it. Here in the north of India, if katha is said, people understand. Let there be two people, and this same talk keeps going. And for this reason, by the power of the katha, they did not find the pain of the world. They did not even come to know the sorrow of the world. The experience was far away. They had no knowledge at all of what the sorrow of the world is. In itself they do not have the sorrow of the world. They are on a ground that is not material. And in this way also they stayed in joy, stayed in happiness. No sorrow from other beings, from the gods, or from oneself came, because of the katha. On this subject Srila Prabhupada writes, what fruit comes from studying the katha of Krishna in the Bhagavatam, or from discussing it, is told in this verse. It is at once captured in the heart by the fortunate and by those eager to hear, at that very moment. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 1.1.2] Nanda Maharaj and Yashoda. We can all be happy simply by discussing the activities of Krishna. The direct yoga of devotion to the Lord, which puts an end to what is unwanted, for people who do not know it, the learned one composed the scripture of the devotees. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 1.7.6] They understand. The translation is not required. Vyasadeva gave this literature so that every person may understand his own transcendental position simply by discussing the Bhagavatam. Prabhupada is pressing on the Bhagavatam. Now, at this moment, everywhere, everyone can be free of the heavy burden and of material troubles by following the Bhagavatam. Cleansing the mirror of the heart, let the sankirtan of Sri Krishna be supremely victorious. [Siksastaka 1] By our Krishna consciousness movement we are distributing the Bhagavatam, so that any person in any part of the world may be absorbed in the pastimes of Krishna by chanting and hearing, and be free from all material troubles. For freedom from all sorrow there is the Bhagavatam, and there is the name of the Lord. Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare. Hare Rama, Hare Rama, Rama Rama, Hare Hare. All of these stayed engaged only in the katha of Krishna and Balarama. They did not make a plan and hold an assembly. Night and day they talked of them, sang, thought. And for this reason they had no sorrow. Situations of sorrow kept coming, and from the katha of the Lord the sorrow did not come.

9
00:39:11,750 --> 00:42:43,640
They completed their kumara age in Braj. This is the lila done in the kumara age, and it will be told later also. It is ahead. But here he is making a kind of close. In this way. By the sports of children in Vraja, they passed the kumara age. They left the kumara age, they spent it. The meaning of the saying is, although Sri Krishna's kumara age was not finished, in three or four years they began to look like children of five, both brothers. They spent the childhood. By the sports of childhood. The sports proper to the kumara age. Which ones. Nilayana. Nilayana means to become absorbed, to hide. To play hide and seek. They would usually hide. Some child would search. Hiding in the corner of a tree, hiding in the house, in a thicket. The game of hide and seek. All this is given in the plural. It is not the sport of one day, and it is not of one time only. In one day they would hide in thousands of ways. And sometimes they would bind a bridge. On the small streams. Not on the great rivers. The small springs that fell in Braj, the little sources of water, on those they would make a dam. The children, saying Jai Sri Rama, would bring a little dust and a little clod. The meaning is, as Lord Rama bound the bridge, so we are binding it. And the children recite Hanuman, the monkeys. Even half a kilo, if they lifted it and brought it, then Jai Sri Rama. And with a roar, in their own understanding, they bring a heavy mountain. This binding of the bridge is also in the plural. So every day the binding of a bridge keeps going in many ways. They were learning. One acharya says, the habit is of binding a bridge in the avatara of Rama, so they are doing it here. Now no ocean is found here. Otherwise they would do it there also. Keep making the dam. And jumping like a monkey. Swinging from one branch to another, going by a leap. Like a monkey. Swinging on the limb of any tree, going like a rope, jumping. By all these sports Lord Krishna and Balarama were spending their kumara age in Braj.

10
00:42:55,530 --> 00:47:43,020
Om namo bhagavate vasudevaya. Sri Shuka said. One day, having fixed the mind on a meal in the forest, rising early from Vraja, waking the friends and the calves with the beautiful sound of the horn, Hari went out with the calves in front. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.12.1] In the next chapter is the katha of the killing of Aghasura. The younger brother of Baki and of Baka. Aghasura was the younger brother of Bakasura and of Putana. The names were very short. Baki, Baka, and the younger name. And they were very dreadful demons. Shukadeva Goswami says, once, at some time. The Lord woke very early. It is the lila of the time when they were grazing the calves. It is a lila of the kumara age. They were still three and a half or four years. Inside of five years. One day Sri Krishna woke very early. Rising in the morning. Every day they woke later, because they were children. The cows would have given milk to the calves. It came in the mind, let us take the calves early, and the cows will come later. There, as they say in Bhojpuri, they will come out to the boundary. There the cows will be milked later. And in the early morning itself they want to go taking the calves. For a meal in the forest. Thinking, we will eat in the forest itself, they went. Then their mother Yashoda and Rohini, rising in the very early morning, when they began to go at dawn, made a great deal of food and bound it and gave it. In the hanging basket. In a clay pot, in which yogurt had been set, very beautiful, she put that in the basket. Not in a pot of tin. Krishna ate from a clay pot. They had taken it. And rice, fresh. And with it chili, ginger, lemon. Pickle also. For eating outside also. And there were sweets too. In Braj not much vegetable was made. There is no great mention of it. There was so much milk, yogurt, and ghee that everything happened from that. In a very beautiful way they took the food. For a meal in the forest. They took the picnic itself as their greatest festival. People cook here and there and eat outside the house. There was no cooking to do. It was the food of the house. But having thought of eating in the forest, he fixed the mind. Krishna bound it in the mind, he decided, today we eat in the forest.

11
00:47:45,450 --> 00:53:24,880
The time for the children to wake had not yet come. But Sri Krishna had already thought in his mind of the forest meal. So, with the beautiful sound of the horn. Charu means beautiful. With the beautiful sound of the horn, going from house to house of the children, he began to wake them. In that horn he will have been speaking as if singing. And placing their names, of his own friends, how beautiful it will have felt. Shukadeva Goswami called this a beautiful sound. Taking up the horn of a cow that had died its own death, he is blowing it. Small horns. And covered with gold. In many ways, with craft, the horns had been decorated. The horn and the stick, to threaten the cows, to threaten the calves. Not for beating. They only showed them. So the stick, the horn, and the flute. Taking these, they went. And the things of the meal they had hung like that on the stick, behind. Their own meal is to be eaten there, so they had hung it on the back. When the Lord has gone to keep cows, he has in truth become a cowherd. He is not doing a play. They are eating in the forest. At home they cannot eat so early. And keep this in mind. The Lord does not take tea in the early morning. Now people make tea family by family, and they give it to the children also to drink. From now they are spoiling the habit. They themselves are spoiled. They give the children tea to drink also. The Lord ate nothing at home. He began to wake the children. With the beautiful sound of the horn. All are independent. They will go on time. But the Lord woke them. They recognized, it is Krishna's voice. They rose, we will go quickly. Then their mothers also, very quickly, wait, wait, quickly preparing the food, began to give it. From every house, sweets, yogurt, milk. Binding it all, they began to give it to the children. They began to bring them to mix with Krishna's calves. And when Sri Krishna came out, bringing out the calves of his own house. Shukadeva is saying Krishna's calves were innumerable. Countless calves. Countless means a number that cannot be counted. Srila Prabhupada, writing on this, says the meaning is hundreds of thousands. A lakh, a crore, an arab, a kharab. However many, it cannot be given a limit. They were grazing calves, so the gods also, becoming calves, had all come. To stay with the Lord. If one is a human being, that is there. Raskhan says, let me live in the village of the cowherd girls of Gokula in Braj. If I am an animal, then where shall I live. Graze me among the cows of Nanda. O Lord, if you make me an animal, then make me one among the cows of Nanda Maharaj. I will graze. Krishna will graze me. So however many devotees there are, the Lord says Krishna, all of them had become calves, by the Lord's mercy. And they were walking. So, innumerable. Srila Prabhupada says this same thing, the calves were countless. So Sri Krishna was waking them, and he was driving the calves. Slowly. The calves do not come out in a great hurry. They would bring the calves and mix them into Krishna's calves. By this one acharya has said, one's own Gokula should be mixed into the Lord's Gokula. One's own senses should be engaged in giving happiness to the Lord's senses. One should not stay in the service of one's own senses. With one's own senses one should serve the senses of the Lord. This is the feeling.

12
00:53:25,540 --> 00:57:48,750
Hari went out, with the calves in front. Why is he being called Hari at this time. They have woken in the morning. The name that has come as the chief among those names. So in the mahamantra, Hare Hare is the more. Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare. Hare Rama, Hare Rama, Rama Rama, Hare Hare. From Hari, Hare. The calves in front. He went out in a special way. Compared with other days, today he went out specially, from his own house and from Gokula. From the settlement, from the village. The meaning of samutthaya, Sanatana Goswami says, when the Lord rose from the bed, he rose properly. The meaning of rising properly is, he opened the eyes very well. After that he washed his face. He washed the hair, he arranged it. In the morning, in the light of the lamp. This is called rising properly. And at once he changed the cloth of the night. Or he bathed. After that they will not have bathed yet. They are not that fixed in the rule, in childhood. But samutthaya is telling us this: he washed the face, he saw his face in the mirror, and he rose. And he began to say only, for going. We have to go, we have to go. Together with him, the little boys, by the thousand. With him, with Krishna, they joined. By the thousand. Prithuka. The children are called prithuka. Prithuka has another meaning also. When children stay small, they stay a little plump, so they are called prithuka. They stay healthy. At that time no child has jaundice or a fever. The children, coming out of their own houses, went out of Vraja together with Krishna. The calves were being mixed with the calves, but the children would come and stand with Krishna. How beautiful their morning arati will have been. To see the Lord, to meet him, to embrace him, and after that to walk slowly. From another house another child is coming out. Coming. Each child wants, I am with Krishna. The children became many, and still, together with him alone. Sakam means together. With Krishna himself. On this the commentary is made that each child is trying this, let me walk pressed close to Krishna. Krishna should not have to be carried at the neck. They did not want to give him labor. Krishna keeps only the stick, the horn, and the flute, and they took those, they looked after them. Each child wanted this, walk with Krishna. Then the question comes here. Shukadeva Goswami knows that all the children cannot be with Krishna, so why is he saying together with him. In the mind of the children there is this wish, let me walk with Krishna. So Krishna also, as many friends as there are, is walking with them in that many forms. And each child knows only this, I am walking with Krishna. This is the experience of all. So the words together with him alone are used.

13
00:57:50,900 --> 01:04:06,610
Affectionate. And all were snigdha, glossy with affection. All were supreme lovers of Krishna. One in whom there is affection, he is called snigdha. A very beautiful stick, and a beautiful flute, and a beautiful basket. Four things. The su, the beautiful, will apply to all. A beautiful basket, a beautiful stick, a beautiful horn, a beautiful flute. The rods were so beautiful that they were worth looking at. Small. As large as the children's bodies were, that large they kept the rods. Small rods. Thin. They will have kept them smaller than their own size. So, su. They speak of the marks on the basket. From this, the effort. Everyone will know what a chhika is. It is made of rope. A pot is kept on it. From the fear of ants, or from the fear of a cat, or of another. In the thatch, in the ceiling, it is kept hanging. And the cat also keeps looking, and it cannot reach. For the children, baskets had been made of very beautiful silk cord. Special, for all. Not of a very hard rope. Very beautiful. So Srila Shukadeva Goswami, considering, says su. Very beautiful baskets, and the stick, the horn, and the flute. All together, many flutes have come to be with them. They were very beautiful. Wherever the eye is cast, all beautiful, beautiful, beautiful. Putting su in one place. Su means well, beautiful. Every thing very beautiful. He is not able to go further. How beautiful they are. When the articles with them are so beautiful, then how beautiful those children are. And there is Krishna. Then, their own, more than even their thousands. They kept mixing their own calves, more than even thousands, into Krishna's calves. In going to the forest, there is no thought now that the calves will walk separately. The calves of the families would mix into Krishna's calves. These calves also wanted to walk with Krishna's calves. All wanted this, Krishna will graze us, Krishna will drive us. Coming, they kept joining in happiness. See what a good nature this is. Otherwise the animals here are such that one animal will not let another join. So it was said ahead of Krishna, let them be mixed into Krishna's calves. In this way they went. With joy. With supreme joy. They went with great happiness. Not one child was feeling, he woke us this early. No. What, it was early. They were in great joy that so early the meeting with the Lord had happened, and they would stay together the whole day. A great deal of time was found for staying near Krishna. And no one is asking, why did you wake so early. Why are you going so early. No one asked. And they were in joy. On some days the children would come even at midnight to Nanda Baba's house. They would say, Krishna, the time has come. Come, come. Then Mother would tell them, this is the time. Go, sleep. It is only midnight now. When the children would turn toward the grazing, sleep would not come to them. In the separation from Krishna they would go home greatly unhappy. Then someone's sleep would break at ten. Someone's at eleven. Then he would come running, the time has come, morning has come, let us go to the forest. In this way Krishna's company will be found.

14
01:04:06,610 --> 01:07:58,000
When the Lord sends Uddhava to Braj, the gopis say, we have understood why he does not come to Braj. This is the fear. The herder would bring the cows. From this fear he has not come, that the children will again wake him at midnight, and again send him to graze the cows. And perhaps he will also have this fear, that the gopis will again call him a thief, and again have him bound by Yashoda, have him beaten. Thinking of this pain, he is not coming. And Uddhava, go and tell him, now no one will speak. We have kept our yogurt in such a way that Krishna may come and eat. Now no one will speak. And we have taken acceptance from Mother Yashoda. She keeps weeping, she says, now I will not bind, now I will not beat, whatever he does. One pot, or let him break thousands. They are taking him, waking and waking, so why not. Muda. Muda is a word in Sanskrit. Of the great sage. And it is in the third case, with joy. They went from joy. They are walking in joy. With Krishna's countless calves, making their own calves into one pair, into one herd, all are walking. And grazing, and with other lilas. They came out of the village, and the grazing of the calves began. They were hungry through the night, so they began to graze. And they began to wander in this way. Krishna is with these friends, and there are other lilas also. As children play, so they were grazing while playing. Not standing and grazing with great worry, that someone's field not be grazed. The calves began to graze, and the lilas on the earth began. What lilas would happen, Shukadeva will now tell us. Here and there, indeed. The meaning of ha is, indeed, it is famous. This was a completely famous thing, a thing known to all, that the moment the calves began to graze, these people began to play.

